The issue is FutureWarning about default numeric_only in DataFrameGroupBy.mean. In pivot_table, aggfunc default is "mean". After grouping, they call grouped.agg(aggfunc). In pandas GroupBy.agg when aggfunc is string 'mean', it maps to GroupBy.mean (maybe). That method now raises warning about numeric_only default. To suppress or provide argument numeric_only, they need to pass numeric_only parameter when calling mean.

GroupBy.agg with string 'mean' likely uses aggregation dispatch that calls the mean method without numeric_only; perhaps they can change to pass numeric_only=False or True depending.

Solution likely to modify pivot_table internal function to call grouped.mean(numeric_only=True?) but need preserve behavior. Future warning says default numeric_only depreciation; default will become False; mean currently default numeric_only=True? Actually pandas 1.5.1: GroupBy.mean default numeric_only=True? I think they want to keep current behavior which excludes non-numeric columns. In pivot_table default would compute mean of numeric columns only. So passing numeric_only=True replicates current behavior. So modify __internal_pivot_table to compute agg differently: if aggfunc is string 'mean' and not a callable, they could use grouped.mean(numeric_only=True) instead of agg. But also need for other string functions like 'sum'? Those also might have numeric_only warnings (maybe). Could handle generic case: if isinstance(aggfunc, str), use getattr(grouped, aggfunc)(numeric_only=True) if that method supports numeric_only else grouped.agg(aggfunc).

Simpler: change the line agged = grouped.agg(aggfunc) to use grouped.aggregate(..., numeric_only=True)?? Actually agg doesn't accept numeric_only.

Thus implement conditional before: if isinstance(aggfunc, str):
    # try to call the method directly with numeric_only parameter
    func = getattr(grouped, aggfunc, None)
    if callable(func):
        try:
            agged = func(numeric_only=True)
        except TypeError:
            agged = grouped.agg(aggfunc)
    else:
        agged = grouped.agg(aggfunc)
else:
    agged = grouped.agg(aggfunc)

